# Nixploy — core rules

Self-hosted PaaS. pnpm monorepo: `apps/web` (Next.js 16 +
Tailwind v4 + shadcn/ui, custom `server.ts` with WebSockets/deploy queue/crons),
`apps/cli`, `packages/server` (Drizzle schema, better-auth, tRPC routers, deploy
engine). Marketing: `apps/landing` → https://nixploy.com, whose UI is vendored
from component registries (`components.json`; `src/components/ui/**` is
third-party — Biome and knip skip it). Full guides in `docs/`,
agent rules in `AGENTS.md`.

## Non-negotiables

- Biome style: tabs, double quotes, named exports. Run
  `pnpm exec biome check --write <files>` from the repo root before finishing.
- Typecheck after changes: `pnpm -F @nixploy/server exec tsc --noEmit` and/or
  `cd apps/web && pnpm exec tsc --noEmit`.
- Tests: `pnpm test` (vitest in packages/server) must stay green.
- No `child_process` in feature code — use `execAsync` / `execAsyncRemote(serverId)`.
- No hardcoded `/etc/nixploy` — resolve via `paths.ts` helpers (`NIXPLOY_CONFIG_DIR`).
- Secrets only in `encryptedText` columns (AES, `ENCRYPTION_KEY`).
- New DB fields: edit Drizzle schema → `pnpm db:generate` → commit migration.
- Minimal diffs; match surrounding code style; no speculative abstractions.
- Do not run `pnpm install` inside a single workspace package — install at the
  repo root so workspace symlinks stay intact.

## Tenancy

organization → project → environment → service (application, compose,
postgres, mysql, mariadb, mongo, redis). Every tenant-scoped procedure
resolves the org with `resolveCallerOrganizationId(userId, activeOrganizationId)`
from `modules/projects` (async, falls back to first membership) and filters
rows by it. Never read `session.activeOrganizationId` raw, never throw on it
being null.
